   "evidence": "Density/Basic.lean:90-92 defines it in `namespace Nucleus`; Nuclei/Basic.lean:8 imports only `Mathlib.Data.Nat.Notation`. Roadmap \u00a70.3 (`README.md:361-372`, `Suggested.lean:170-172` `moment_rescaling` divides by `nuc.mass`) and \u00a70.4 (`upCount`/`downCount`, `Suggested.lean:194-197`) need `(A:\u211d) \u2260 0`/`0 < (A:\u211d)` and live under `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/Nuclear/` (README.md:97-98), which has no reason to import the density stack.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Density/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Move `cast_massNumber_pos` (and, if wanted, a `cast_massNumber_ne_zero`) to `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Basic.lean`, adding the cheap `Mathlib.Data.Nat.Cast.Order.Basic`-level import there; keep it public.",
   "issue": "`Nucleus.cast_massNumber_pos : (0:\u211d) < nuc.massNumber` is a fact about `Nucleus` alone \u2014 nothing in its statement or proof touches densities, `Space`, or measure theory \u2014 yet it is only reachable by importing this module, which pulls in Physlib `Space`, `MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner.Basic`, Gaussian and Haar material. `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Basic.lean` is the canonical home and currently exports no real-cast API at all.",
